# Pickled extraction output. Untracked deliberately: loading a pickle executes
# the code inside it, so a committed pickle is an executable stored as data
# (STATUS.md section 6, trap 2). The files stay on disk — they were untracked
# with `git rm --cached`, never `git rm`.
# NOTE: tests/*.pkl is NOT covered here. Three scripts under tests/ read those,
# and they remain tracked.
cache/

# NOTE, 2026-10-08, on the user's instruction: `10K_filings/` and `extractions/`
# are now TRACKED. They were ignored as "data", which is a tidiness reason and not
# a safety one, and the cost of that was measured twice:
#   - backlog item 117: the only test of a real route B file is `skipif`-guarded on
#     `extractions/WMT.json`, so it ran on no clean checkout.
#   - backlog item 140: the mutation that would empty `P14g-unit-statement-pages`
#     survives the whole suite on any machine without `10K_filings/`, in silence.
# A guard that is absent on every machine but one is not a guard. 33 MB, 10 files,
# largest 11.6 MB, all public SEC documents that never change once filed.
#
# `cache/` below stays ignored and the reason there IS a safety one. Do not
# group them together again.

# macOS
.DS_Store

# NOTE: `CLAUDE.md` used to be listed here, but the file is tracked, so the line
# did nothing except mislead — git does not ignore a tracked file. CLAUDE.md is
# now the entry point to docs/INDEX.md and is deliberately tracked.
# To untrack it instead: `git rm --cached CLAUDE.md` and re-add the line.
